        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: St. Mary's School, Pune; Community of St Mary the Virgin\n- Places: Pune, India; Wantage, Oxfordshire, England\n- People: Reverend William John Butler\n- Concepts: Anglican religious orders; Church of England\n\nFacts:\n- The Community of St Mary the Virgin was founded in 1848 by the Reverend William John Butler, the vicar of Wantage.\n- The Community of St Mary the Virgin is an Anglican religious order based at Wantage in Oxfordshire, England.\n- The Community of St Mary the Virgin is one of the oldest surviving religious communities in the Church of England.\n- St. Mary's School, Pune, India, was founded in 1866 to educate the daughters of officers of the British Indian Army posted to Pune.\n- From 1866 to 1977, St. Mary's School, Pune, was run by the Sisters of the Community of St Mary the Virgin, an Anglican order based in Wantage, England.",
